.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-UNSUBSCRIBE 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-unsubscribe \- deletes a subscription
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens unsubscribe
.BR \-\-subscription | \-s
.I SUBSCRIPTION-ERN
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a subscription, identified by the ERN returned by
.BR euclid-cli-ens-subscribe (1).
Once deleted, messages published to the subscription's topic are no longer
delivered to its target. Deleting an ERN with no matching subscription is
not an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-subscription " " \fISUBSCRIPTION-ERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the subscription to delete. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The subscription was deleted (or was already absent). No output is
printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, or the server could not be reached.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens unsubscribe \e
    --subscription ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:subscription:6f1b1e2e...
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-subscribe (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
